{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause from evidence (AC1), 2026-11-12. Runs 41918750684 and 43105554680 both fail at POST /update_jobs/<id>/create_pull_request -> 400 \"invalid or unauthorized changes\". The latest log shows the uv job running `uv pip compile --output-file=.github/release-requirements.txt ... .github/release-requirements.in` (twice), i.e. the uv scan treats .github/release-requirements.{in,txt} as pip manifests and puts the recompiled .github file into the uv-lock group. The only file the group touches outside uv.lock/pyproject.toml is under .github/, and public reports tie this exact 400 to non-actions ecosystems changing files under .github/ (laazyj/composureCDK#651, shyden-labs/shyden.co.uk#1118, athob/py-EnBiD-ananke#12; cleared by moving or excluding them), with a counterexample noted in glsec/glsec.github.io#43. GitHub has not confirmed the mechanism, so this is the leading supported cause, tested by the fix.\nHANDOFF STATE 06:00 PST: fix committed in .rebar/worktrees/fix-dependabot as 518f46f166d (with eagleeyed-lexical-midge), not pushed: `exclude-paths: [\".github/**\"]` on the uv entry (documented option; note dependabot-core#15102 reports the uv dependency-graph builder ignoring it). GitHub reruns Dependabot whenever dependabot.yml changes, so the merge itself triggers the run AC2 needs. Next: make verify, push, merge, read the triggered run."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794491840561009029,"uuid":"c45132e8-40b6-4c37-96cf-d96dc97b2a25"}